r#  99316  1884  59
p: .
t. 
|   Since conceptual syntheses are
|  reshuffled with almost every word, we are
|  invoking staging faculties at almost every
|  step, such that sentence-understanding is intrinsically a
|  process that swings back and forth between
|  extralinguistic and syntactic/semantic/pragmatic
|  inference.  Against this backdrop, I think I can more rigorously
|  defend my earlier-stated objection to the
.  idea (explicit or not) that sentences signify propositions


--- Sentence/switch
id: 569
r#  99317  1884  60


--- Sentence//end
id: 569
r#  99482  1888  10
p: .
t. 
|  Discourse may indeed communicate beliefs,
|  but that phenomenon emerges from a multifaceted
|  process integrating both linguistic and extralinguistic
.  ideations


