p: .
t. 
|  To draw once again from coding analogies,
|  programming language semantics is concerned with the binding
|  of values to symbols --- when those markings start and
|  cease to be appropriate --- as well as polymorphic
|  definition of multiple procedures with the \clrmr{17}{112}same symbol
|  but different parameter types, and other type-related
.  concerns


--- Sentence/switch
id: 592
r#  104383  1983  10


--- Sentence//end
id: 592
r#  104710  1988  21
p: .
t. 
|   Code syntax addresses such issues as
|  expression boundaries, storage-duration scope, and sequence points, indicating
|  which values are parameters for which function-calls as
|  well as, potentially, the order of procedures' side-effects
|  (particularly when a prior effect could be visible to
.  a future subroutine)


